   "defaults": {
    "safeAreaCount": 1,
    "safeAreaSize": 0.25,
    "safeZone": "STATIC"
   },
   "notes": "The floor turns hostile except for a refuge. STATIC places the patch once and asks whether the player can reach it; MOVING walks the patch along a closed path and asks whether they can keep up; QUADRANT halves or quarters the arena and rotates which part is safe, so the crossing is made on the pulse. A moving patch may never outrun the player and a rotating one owes a full walk to the next part, both floored by fairness."
  },
