   "notes": "A thin chain whip. Line layouts (SLASH, BACKSLASH, CROSS, ZIGZAG, SNAKE, CORRIDOR, POLYLINE) make the chain itself the danger -- dodging is precise positioning off the line. CORRIDOR draws parallel chains around a safe channel floored by the fairness system. LANE is the legacy direction whip: the chain claims one lane of a tiling that covers the arena."
  },
