    "sweepDirection": "CW",
    "skipStep": 0,
    "firstAngleDeg": -90,
    "startSector": 0,
    "innerRadius": 0
   },
   "notes": "The arena cut into wedges that go off in turn. There is always a safe majority, so the ask is pacing rather than precision: keep circling at the sweep's speed. `sweepDirection` sets CW/CCW, `skipStep` leaves safe wedges between activations, and the sweep may never advance faster than the player can walk the rim -- the step is floored by both reachability and warning, so a fast tempo lengthens the sequence instead of tightening it."
  },
